<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Chinese Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1931 CE – 1937 CE · capital Ruijin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Communist state founded in the hills of Jiangxi in 1931, where Mao Zedong and the Red Army learned to govern before the Long March.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nationalist-government">Nationalist government</a> turned on its Communist allies in 1927, Communist forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> and Zhu De built rural bases in the mountains between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangxi">Jiangxi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a>. On 7 November 1931 a congress at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruijin">Ruijin</a> proclaimed the Chinese Soviet Republic, with Mao as chairman of its central executive committee.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic redistributed land from landlords to poor peasants, issued its own currency, stamps and laws on marriage and labour, and mobilised villagers for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-red-army">Red Army</a>. It was linked to other soviet base areas across central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Its policies were shaped by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-international">Comintern</a>-trained leaders, who sidelined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao</a> after 1932, and by constant encirclement campaigns launched by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The fifth encirclement campaign, using blockhouses and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a>, broke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangxi">Jiangxi</a> base, and in October 1934 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-red-army">Red Army</a> began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/long-march">Long March</a>, reaching northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a> in 1935. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-united-front">Second United Front</a> in 1937 the remaining soviet became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaan-gan-ning-border-region">Shaan-Gan-Ning Border Region</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chinese-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Chinese Soviet Republic" width="320" height="231"><figcaption>Image: Own work (Ericmetro) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:National_Flag_of_Chinese_Soviet_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1931 CE – 1937 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ruijin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mao Zedong, Zhu De (commander)</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>State atheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hakka, Gan, Mandarin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jiangxi Soviet</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=chinese-soviet-republic" aria-label="Chinese Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7748 1226 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chinese Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8068 1482L8221 1549"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8221 1549h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8068 1482h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8068 1482h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ruijin. <a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=chinese-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
